(BAS-34 - only function definitions can span multiple sentences. A loop
 cannot: the period ends the While, and the next sentence is top-level,
 so it runs once after the loop rather than three times inside it.
 Contrast BAS-19, where a function body made of three separate sentences
 stays one construct until the blank line.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-34.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   a new sentence, not the loop body
   3
)
a number called x is 0.
While x is less than 3, increment x.
print "a new sentence, not the loop body".
print x.
